<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scrovegni Chapel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1305</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Arena Chapel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Scrovegni Chapel in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a> was built for the banker Enrico Scrovegni and consecrated in 1305. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giotto">Giotto</a> covered its interior with a fresco cycle of the lives of the Virgin and Christ and the Last Judgement, under a deep blue vault. It is one of the most important works of Western painting and part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scrovegni-chapel.jpg" alt="Scrovegni Chapel" width="320" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zairon · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Padova_Cappella_degli_Scrovegni_Innen_Langhaus_West_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
